It defines the order in which Python searches for
methods and attributes in inheritance, especially in multiple inheritance.

Why MRO is needed?

Suppose a class inherits from multiple parent classes, and multiple parents have the same method.

Python needs rules to decide:

“Which method should I call first?”

MRO solves this problem.

One-line Interview Answer:
MRO (Method Resolution Order) defines the sequence in which Python searches parent classes
 for methods and attributes, especially during multiple inheritance.

Real Importance of MRO

MRO is very important in:
Multiple inheritance
Frameworks
Mixins
super()
Large object-oriented systems